      "body": "Full message (please include it when possible):\n\n```\nException ignored in the internal traceback machinery:\nAttributeError: 'object' object has no attribute '_print_exception_bltin'\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/bswck/Python/cpython/t.py\", line 12, in <module>\npython: Objects/call.c:618: callmethod: Assertion `callable != NULL' failed.\nFatal Python error: Aborted\nAborted (core dumped)\n```\n\nThe problem happens because `_Py_FindSourceFile` resorts to `_PyObject_CallMethodFormat` which assumes `callable` is healthy (the `callable` in this case is the result of getting `open` of `io`, which is `NULL` because `io` is an `object()` from `test_import`).\nMaybe NULL-check the `callable` first? (PR in progress)\n",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
