      "created_at": "2025-12-15T13:58:23Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-12-15T13:58:23Z",
      "body": "> Maybe NULL-check the callable first? (PR in progress)\n\nI think the issue is here:\n\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/blob/14d3974db01b6c4b14a4829b4310b2511993aa8e/Python/traceback.c#L417-L420\n\nWe need to check for a `NULL` result from `PyObject_GetAttr`, not defer the check to `_PyObject_CallMethodFormat`, because:\n\n1. That will slow things down for other callers.\n2. It's generally unsafe to call arbitrary C API functions with an exception set.",
